## Explanation

This diagram shows the **investigation graph structure** — the core data model for causal attack reconstruction.

### Entity-Relationship Model

| Entity | Table | Key Relationships |
|--------|-------|-------------------|
| `Investigation` | `investigations` | Root aggregate; owns all child entities |
| `EvidenceNode` | `evidence` | One per evidence object; nodes in graph |
| `CorrelationEdge` | `correlations` | Directed edges between evidence nodes |
| `Finding` | `findings` | Detection conclusions with evidence citations |
| `Hypothesis` | `hypotheses` | Analyst theories with confidence tracking |
| `Timeline` | `timelines` | Ordered event sequences for export |

### Graph Implementation (petgraph)

```rust
use petgraph::graph::Graph;
use petgraph::Direction;
use petgraph::visit::EdgeRef;

type InvestigationGraph = Graph<EvidenceNode, CorrelationEdge, Directed>;

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
struct EvidenceNode {
    evidence_id: String,
    evidence_type: String,  // "artifact/process", "artifact/file", etc.
    timestamp: DateTime<Utc>,
    summary: String,        // Human-readable: "Process: powershell.exe (PID 200)"
    metadata: Value,        // Full evidence metadata
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
struct CorrelationEdge {
    relation: String,       // "spawned", "wrote", "connected", etc.
    confidence: f32,        // 0.0 - 1.0
    method: String,         // "pid_link", "file_write", "net_link", etc.
    details: Value,         // Method-specific details
    evidence_ids: Vec<String>, // Supporting evidence IDs for this edge
}
```

